 "intro": [
  "The twelve sons of Jacob, the fathers of the tribes of Israel, are born to four mothers: Leah and Rachel, and their maidservants Zilpah and Bilhah. Each name is explained by the mother's words at the birth, many of them prayers. Dinah is the only daughter named.",
  "The short line beside each name gives the meaning the text itself draws from it."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Rashi on Genesis 29–30 and 35; Genesis Rabbah 70–73; Babylonian Talmud, Berakhot 7b and 60a.",
